      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Noel sits on the Elk River, with Butler and Mill creeks, and the river flows northwest into the Neosho River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noel%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The rolling Ozark hills surround Noel, and the Noel bluffs were carved by the Elk River centuries ago, giving the town a unique landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://4noel.com/tourist.html",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Noel’s Christmas‑themed name draws thousands of holiday cards each year, with the USPS Noel Post Office stamping them “Noel, Mo.”.",
